IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wk-nouns`
IMPORT `wk-agreements`
IMPORT `wk-information`
IMPORT `wk-restrictive-terms`
IMPORT `wk-contractors-and-claims`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for the encoding of the Antitrust Guidelines for Business Activities
-- Affecting Workers (DOJ and FTC, revised January 2025). Agency enforcement policy, not
-- law (n.1 [pdf page 2]).
--
-- Written by an independent test author who read the source text first and wrote the
-- answers down (scratchpad answers.md, sha256 ba5f270c..., frozen 2026-11-25T17:31:46Z)
-- before opening this folder. Only the nouns and the output vocabularies of the rule
-- modules were read to learn the names; the encoding's own tests were not read. Each
-- group cites the provision and the [pdf page N] marker of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/2025-business-activities-affecting-workers-guidelines.txt.
-- Row ids (G1, S1a, F15a, ...) are the rows of answers.md.
--
-- A failing assertion here is a finding and is left failing on purpose.
--
-- Target: main. Lists are compared by membership (elem), never by order, except where
-- an assertion compares the same function's output on two inputs that differ only in a
-- fact the text says does not matter.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      s IS AN a
      r IS A MAYBE (LIST OF a)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind says` s r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST l THEN elem s l

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      r IS A MAYBE (LIST OF a)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind nothing or empty` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST l THEN
        CONSIDER l
        WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
        WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN FALSE

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      l IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind is empty` l MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN FALSE

-- Short names for the sentences asserted below (the encoding's own values).
`ind s1 crime` MEANS `businesses that compete with each other for workers may be committing an antitrust crime if they enter into such an agreement`
`ind s1 civil` MEANS `even if criminal charges are not pursued, such an agreement may also be subject to civil liability`
`ind s1 illegal even if` MEANS `the agencies state that such an agreement, formed between competing or potentially competing employers, directly or through an intermediary, is illegal even if it did not result in actual harm such as lower wages`
`ind s1 n15` MEANS `n.15: such an agreement may require a fuller analysis of its effects, the restraint being subordinate and collateral to a broader business collaboration and reasonably necessary to achieve its procompetitive potential`
`ind s1 starting point` MEANS `an agreement to set a starting point for compensation may be a form of wage fixing under the law`
`ind s1 DOJ felony` MEANS `the DOJ may criminally investigate and, where appropriate, bring felony charges against the participants in such an agreement, including both individuals and companies`

`ind fx s1` MEANS `section 1: the agencies state that such an agreement is illegal even if it did not result in actual harm such as lower wages`
`ind fx n15` MEANS `n.15: such an agreement may require a fuller analysis of its effects`
`ind fx s2` MEANS `section 2: the agencies state that such an agreement can be per se illegal, and may be illegal regardless of whether it actually harms workers`
`ind fx s6` MEANS `section 6: such an agreement may constitute the type of per se violation of the antitrust laws that exposes the platforms to criminal liability`

`ind s2 scrutiny` MEANS `no-poach clauses in franchise agreements are subject to antitrust scrutiny`
`ind s2 per se` MEANS `the agencies state that such an agreement between a franchisor and its franchisee not to compete for workers can be per se illegal under the antitrust laws: the agreement itself may be illegal regardless of whether it actually harms workers`
`ind s2 organizing` MEANS `a franchisor may violate the antitrust laws by organizing or enforcing a no-poach agreement among franchisees that compete for workers`
`ind s2 other laws` MEANS `agreements among franchisees, either written or unwritten, not to poach, hire, or solicit each other's workers may violate other federal and state laws`

`ind s3 headline` MEANS `sharing competitively sensitive information with competitors about terms and conditions of employment may violate the antitrust laws`
`ind s3 effect found` MEANS `exchanging competitively sensitive compensation or other employment information with a competitor may be unlawful when the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect, whether or not that effect was intended: such an effect is found`
`ind s3 effect unassessed` MEANS `exchanging competitively sensitive compensation or other employment information with a competitor may be unlawful when the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect, whether or not that effect was intended: its effect has not been assessed`
`ind s3 algorithm` MEANS `providing competitively sensitive information through an algorithm or through a third party's tool or product may also be unlawful`
`ind s3 recommendations` MEANS `information exchanges facilitated by or through a third party, including through an algorithm or other software, that are used to generate wage or other benefit recommendations can be unlawful even if the exchange does not require businesses to strictly adhere to those recommendations`
`ind s3 discretion` MEANS `an agreement to use shared wage recommendations, lists, calculations, or algorithms can also still be unlawful even where co-conspirators retain some discretion or cheat on the agreement`
`ind s3 joint venture` MEANS `even if the companies are parties to a legitimate transaction or a joint venture or other collaborative activity, an agreement between them to share information about wages or other terms of employment may violate the antitrust laws`

`ind s4 can violate` MEANS `non-compete clauses that restrict workers from switching jobs or starting a competing business can violate the antitrust laws`
`ind s4 federal` MEANS `non-competes may also violate other federal laws, such as the National Labor Relations Act and the Packers and Stockyards Act`
`ind s4 state` MEANS `non-competes can also violate state laws, including laws banning unfair methods of competition and unfair or deceptive practices, as well as statutes banning or restricting some or all non-competes`

`ind s5 NDA antitrust` MEANS `non-disclosure agreements can violate the antitrust laws when they span such a large scope of information that they function to prevent workers from seeking or accepting other work or starting a business after they leave their job`
`ind s5 NDA industry` MEANS `a non-disclosure agreement drafted so broadly as to prohibit disclosure of any information that is usable in or relates to an industry may be unlawful`
`ind s5 NDA federal` MEANS `non-disclosure agreements can also violate federal law when they are worded so broadly as to suggest that workers who report potential violations of law, or who cooperate with a government investigation, could face lawsuits and adverse employment consequences`
`ind s5 TRAP` MEANS `depending on the facts and circumstances, a training repayment agreement provision can be anticompetitive`
`ind s5 non-solicit` MEANS `depending on the facts and circumstances, a non-solicitation agreement that prohibits a worker from soliciting former clients or customers of the employer can be anticompetitive`
`ind s5 exit fee` MEANS `depending on the facts and circumstances, an exit fee or liquidated damages provision can be anticompetitive`
`ind s5 example` MEANS `the provision is the text's own example of when it can be anticompetitive: it functions to prevent the worker from working for another firm, seeking or accepting another job, or starting a business`
`ind s5 indications` MEANS `the agencies may investigate if there are indications that such a restrictive condition on workers is harming competition`

`ind s6 overview` MEANS `the Overview: an agreement between businesses to fix the compensation that each pays to independent contractors may violate the antitrust laws, just as an agreement between businesses to fix the wages each pays to workers may violate the antitrust laws`
`ind s6 platforms` MEANS `an agreement between two or more competing platforms to fix the compensation of independent contractors offering their services via the platforms may constitute the type of per se violation of the antitrust laws that exposes the platforms to criminal liability`

`ind s7 investigate` MEANS `the agencies may investigate and take action against businesses that make false or misleading claims about potential earnings that workers, including both employees and independent contractors, may realize`
`ind s7 UDAP` MEANS `the Overview: false claims about workers' potential earnings may violate federal laws against unfair, deceptive, or abusive practices`

`ind CAARA` MEANS `the Criminal Antitrust Anti-Retaliation Act provides whistleblower protections for employees, contractors, subcontractors, and agents who report antitrust crimes, including no-poach and wage-fixing agreements`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Inputs. Every record field is supplied; where a choice of input was mine, it is said.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      markets IS A LIST OF STRING
      products IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Business`
`ind firm` n markets products MEANS `Business` WITH
    `the name of the business` IS n
    `the labor markets in which it hires or retains workers` IS markets
    `the products or services it makes, sells or provides` IS products

-- Choice: "compete for workers" is represented by a shared labor-market name, which is
-- how the nouns delineate a labor market (the caller's STRING).
`ind A` MEANS `ind firm` "Firm A" (LIST "software engineers, Bay Area") (LIST "search engines")
`ind B` MEANS `ind firm` "Firm B" (LIST "software engineers, Bay Area") (LIST "animated films")
`ind C` MEANS `ind firm` "Firm C" (LIST "poultry plant workers, Delmarva") (LIST "chicken")
`ind plane maker` MEANS `ind firm` "Plane maker" (LIST "aerospace engineers, Seattle") (LIST "airplanes")
`ind parts supplier` MEANS `ind firm` "Parts supplier" (LIST "aerospace engineers, Seattle") (LIST "engine parts")
`ind franchisor` MEANS `ind firm` "Franchisor" (LIST "restaurant crew, Miami") (LIST "burgers")
`ind franchisee 1` MEANS `ind firm` "Franchisee 1" (LIST "restaurant crew, Miami") (LIST "burgers")
`ind franchisee 2` MEANS `ind firm` "Franchisee 2" (LIST "restaurant crew, Miami") (LIST "burgers")
`ind remote franchisee` MEANS `ind firm` "Franchisee in Anchorage" (LIST "restaurant crew, Anchorage") (LIST "burgers")
`ind platform X` MEANS `ind firm` "Platform X" (LIST "delivery drivers, Chicago") (LIST "food delivery app")
`ind platform Y` MEANS `ind firm` "Platform Y" (LIST "delivery drivers, Chicago") (LIST "food delivery app")

GIVEN x IS A `Business`
      y IS A `Business`
      potential IS A BOOLEAN
      jv IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Two businesses`
`ind pair` x y potential jv MEANS `Two businesses` WITH
    `one business` IS x
    `the other business` IS y
    `the businesses are potentially competing employers` IS potential
    `they have some other collaborative or cooperative relationship, such as a joint venture` IS jv

`ind rivals` MEANS `ind pair` `ind A` `ind B` FALSE FALSE
`ind JV partners` MEANS `ind pair` `ind A` `ind B` FALSE TRUE
`ind non-rivals` MEANS `ind pair` `ind A` `ind C` FALSE FALSE
`ind potential rivals` MEANS `ind pair` `ind A` `ind C` TRUE FALSE
`ind plane pair` MEANS `ind pair` `ind plane maker` `ind parts supplier` FALSE FALSE
`ind franchisor and franchisee` MEANS `ind pair` `ind franchisor` `ind franchisee 1` FALSE FALSE
`ind two franchisees` MEANS `ind pair` `ind franchisee 1` `ind franchisee 2` FALSE FALSE
`ind distant franchisees` MEANS `ind pair` `ind franchisee 1` `ind remote franchisee` FALSE FALSE
`ind platforms` MEANS `ind pair` `ind platform X` `ind platform Y` FALSE FALSE

-- G1, G2, and S1's "even if" facts: a formal, express, written, carried-out agreement made
-- by the businesses directly, which caused harm; and its opposite on every count.
`ind formal form` MEANS `Form of the agreement` WITH
    `it is formal` IS TRUE
    `it is express` IS TRUE
    `it is written down` IS TRUE
    `it was spoken or talked about` IS TRUE
    `it was ever carried out` IS TRUE
    `it was made by individuals at the businesses rather than by the businesses themselves` IS FALSE
    `it was entered into through an intermediary` IS FALSE
    `it resulted in actual harm such as lower wages` IS TRUE

`ind informal form` MEANS `Form of the agreement` WITH
    `it is formal` IS FALSE
    `it is express` IS FALSE
    `it is written down` IS FALSE
    `it was spoken or talked about` IS FALSE
    `it was ever carried out` IS FALSE
    `it was made by individuals at the businesses rather than by the businesses themselves` IS TRUE
    `it was entered into through an intermediary` IS TRUE
    `it resulted in actual harm such as lower wages` IS FALSE

GIVEN finding IS A `Finding on whether there is an agreement`
      pair IS A `Two businesses`
      what IS A `What the businesses agree`
      unsolicited IS A BOOLEAN
      workers IS A `Kind of workers concerned`
      platforms IS A BOOLEAN
      franchise IS A `Franchise relationship of the parties`
      organizes IS A BOOLEAN
      subordinate IS A BOOLEAN
      necessary IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `Form of the agreement`
GIVETH AN `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`ind agreement` MEANS `Agreement between businesses relating to workers` WITH
    `the finding on whether there is an agreement` IS finding
    `the businesses` IS pair
    `what the businesses agree` IS what
    `the firms remain allowed to hire workers who apply for a position without first being solicited` IS unsolicited
    `the workers concerned` IS workers
    `the businesses are platforms through which the independent contractors offer their services` IS platforms
    `the franchise relationship of the parties` IS franchise
    `the franchisor organizes or enforces the agreement` IS organizes
    `the restraint is subordinate and collateral to a broader business collaboration, such as a joint venture` IS subordinate
    `the restraint is reasonably necessary to achieve the procompetitive potential of that collaboration` IS necessary
    `the form of the agreement` IS form

`ind fix wages` MEANS `to fix workers' salaries or other terms of compensation or employment, such as bonuses or benefits, at a specific level or within a range`
`ind no hire` MEANS `not to recruit, solicit, hire, or otherwise compete for current, former, or potential workers`
`ind found` MEANS `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses`

-- S1a: competing employers fix a specific wage; the plain case.
`ind wage fixing` MEANS `ind agreement` WITH
    finding IS `ind found`
    pair IS `ind rivals`
    what IS `ind fix wages`
    unsolicited IS FALSE
    workers IS `employees`
    platforms IS FALSE
    franchise IS `no franchise relationship`
    organizes IS FALSE
    subordinate IS FALSE
    necessary IS FALSE
    form IS `ind formal form`

-- G1, G2, S1e, S1k, S1l, S1m: the same agreement, informal, implicit, unwritten, never
-- talked about, never carried out, made by individuals, through an intermediary, no harm.
`ind wage fixing, informal` MEANS `ind agreement` WITH
    finding IS `ind found`
    pair IS `ind rivals`
    what IS `ind fix wages`
    unsolicited IS FALSE
    workers IS `employees`
    platforms IS FALSE
    franchise IS `no franchise relationship`
    organizes IS FALSE
    subordinate IS FALSE
    necessary IS FALSE
    form IS `ind informal form`

-- A no-poach between rivals, with the n.15, competitor and finding facts as parameters.
GIVEN finding IS A `Finding on whether there is an agreement`
      pair IS A `Two businesses`
      what IS A `What the businesses agree`
      unsolicited IS A BOOLEAN
      subordinate IS A BOOLEAN
      necessary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Agreement between businesses relating to workers`
`ind plain` MEANS `ind agreement` WITH
    finding IS finding
    pair IS pair
    what IS what
    unsolicited IS unsolicited
    workers IS `employees`
    platforms IS FALSE
    franchise IS `no franchise relationship`
    organizes IS FALSE
    subordinate IS subordinate
    necessary IS necessary
    form IS `ind formal form`

`ind no-poach` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `ind no hire` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind range agreement` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `to align, stabilize, or otherwise coordinate the wages they set, as by a range, ceiling, or benchmark for calculating wages, without agreeing on a specific wage` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind starting point agreement` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `to set a starting point for compensation` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind partial no-hire` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `to restrict a company's ability to hire another company's workers, without completely prohibiting it` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind no cold call, applicants hireable` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `not to cold call workers` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`ind no cold call, applicants not hireable` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `not to cold call workers` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind permission agreement` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `to request permission from the other company before trying to hire an employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind something else` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind rivals` `something else relating to workers` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind no-poach, non-rivals` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind non-rivals` `ind no hire` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind no-poach, potential rivals` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind potential rivals` `ind no hire` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind wage fixing, potential rivals` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind potential rivals` `ind fix wages` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind no-poach, JV partners, naked` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind JV partners` `ind no hire` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind no-poach, ancillary` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind JV partners` `ind no hire` FALSE TRUE TRUE
`ind wage fixing, ancillary` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind JV partners` `ind fix wages` FALSE TRUE TRUE
`ind no-poach, subordinate not necessary` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind JV partners` `ind no hire` FALSE TRUE FALSE
`ind no-poach, necessary not subordinate` MEANS `ind plain` `ind found` `ind JV partners` `ind no hire` FALSE FALSE TRUE
`ind no-poach, no agreement found` MEANS `ind plain` `the agencies find no agreement between the businesses` `ind rivals` `ind no hire` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind no-poach, agreement undetermined` MEANS `ind plain` `whether there is an agreement has not been determined` `ind rivals` `ind no hire` FALSE FALSE FALSE

