-- Section 7 inputs.
GIVEN false IS A BOOLEAN
      misleading IS A BOOLEAN
      workers IS A `Kind of workers concerned`
GIVETH A `Claim about workers' potential earnings`
`ind claim` MEANS `Claim about workers' potential earnings` WITH
    `the claim is false` IS false
    `the claim is misleading` IS misleading
    `the workers concerned` IS workers

-- Evidence inputs (General principles [pdf page 4]).
GIVEN d IS A BOOLEAN
      p IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      o IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH AN `Evidence of an agreement`
`ind evidence` MEANS `Evidence of an agreement` WITH
    `a business has discussed with another company wages or other potential terms of employment` IS d
    `a business has engaged in parallel behavior that demonstrates a shared understanding` IS p
    `a business has invited another company to participate in a plan to restrict competition for workers, followed by action consistent with that plan` IS i
    `a business has used a common intermediary to obtain competitively sensitive information` IS c
    `other direct or circumstantial evidence offered` IS o

GIVEN r IS A `Role of the person reporting`
      w IS A `What the person reports`
GIVETH A `Report of an antitrust crime`
`ind report` MEANS `Report of an antitrust crime` WITH
    `the role of the person reporting` IS r
    `what the person reports` IS w

-- =======================================================================================
-- G. General principles [pdf pages 3-4]
-- =======================================================================================

-- G1, G2 [pdf pages 3-4]: an agreement "need not be explicit or written down", can be
-- "formal or informal; express or implicit", "need not be written down or talked about at
-- all", and is illegal "even if [it is] never carried out". S1e, S1k, S1l [pdf pages 5-6]:
-- "between individuals at different businesses", "directly or through an intermediary",
-- "even if they did not result in actual harm such as lower wages". So the two forms give
-- the same answer.
#ASSERT `1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind wage fixing, informal` EQUALS `1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind wage fixing`
#ASSERT `General principles: what the text says of whether the agreement's effects matter` `ind wage fixing, informal` EQUALS `General principles: what the text says of whether the agreement's effects matter` `ind wage fixing`

-- G3 [pdf page 4]: the four kinds of evidence the Agencies "may consider".
#ASSERT elem `discussing with another company wages or other potential terms of employment` (`General principles: the kinds of evidence of an agreement that are present` (`ind evidence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY))
#ASSERT elem `parallel behavior that demonstrates a shared understanding` (`General principles: the kinds of evidence of an agreement that are present` (`ind evidence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EMPTY))
