#ASSERT NOT (`ind says` `ind fx n15` (`General principles: what the text says of whether the agreement's effects matter` `ind wage fixing`))

-- S1b [pdf page 5]: "a range, ceiling, or benchmark for calculating wages, it does not
-- matter if they do not agree on a specific wage": still wage-fixing.
#ASSERT `1: what the agreement is, in substance` `to align, stabilize, or otherwise coordinate the wages they set, as by a range, ceiling, or benchmark for calculating wages, without agreeing on a specific wage` EQUALS JUST `a wage-fixing agreement`
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 illegal even if` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind range agreement`)

-- S1c [pdf page 6]: "an agreement to set a starting point for compensation may be a form
-- of wage fixing under the law", after "Nor does it matter if the agreement does not
-- include specific pay rates".
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 starting point` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind starting point agreement`)
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 illegal even if` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind starting point agreement`)

-- S1f [pdf page 5]: not to hire, solicit, or otherwise compete for workers: no-poach.
#ASSERT `1: what the agreement is, in substance` `ind no hire` EQUALS JUST `a no-poach agreement, also called a no-hire, no-solicit, or market allocation agreement`
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 crime` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind no-poach`)
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 illegal even if` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind no-poach`)
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 DOJ felony` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind no-poach`)

-- S1g [pdf pages 5-6]: restricting without completely prohibiting hiring: still no-poach.
#ASSERT `1: what the agreement is, in substance` `to restrict a company's ability to hire another company's workers, without completely prohibiting it` EQUALS JUST `a no-poach agreement, also called a no-hire, no-solicit, or market allocation agreement`
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 illegal even if` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind partial no-hire`)

-- S1h [pdf page 6]: no cold-calling is "a no-solicit agreement regardless of whether the
-- firms are allowed to hire the workers who applied ... without first being solicited".
#ASSERT `1: what the agreement is, in substance` `not to cold call workers` EQUALS JUST `a no-poach agreement, also called a no-hire, no-solicit, or market allocation agreement`
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 illegal even if` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind no cold call, applicants hireable`)
#ASSERT `1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind no cold call, applicants hireable` EQUALS `1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind no cold call, applicants not hireable`

-- S1i [n.11, pdf page 5]: "an agreement to request permission from the other company
-- before trying to hire an employee" is a no-poach agreement.
#ASSERT `1: what the agreement is, in substance` `to request permission from the other company before trying to hire an employee` EQUALS JUST `a no-poach agreement, also called a no-hire, no-solicit, or market allocation agreement`
#ASSERT `ind says` `ind s1 illegal even if` (`1: what section 1 says of the agreement` `ind permission agreement`)

-- S1j [n.11, pdf page 5]: other agreements are not wage-fixing or no-poach. (Input
